    "stem": "Sagar has $28=2^{2}\\times 7$ and $42=2\\times 3\\times 7$. He wants their LCM from these prime factorisations.\n\nWhich plan is correct?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Take each prime at its highest power: $2^{2}\\times 3\\times 7=84$.",
      "B": "Take only the primes that appear in both factorisations: $2\\times 7=14$.",
      "C": "Multiply every printed prime power from both lists without trimming: $2^{2}\\times 7\\times 2\\times 3\\times 7$.",
      "D": "The LCM is $28$, because $28$ is the first number printed."
